Authoring · Tailwind-derived syntax

Inserts the declarations and nested variant rules of utility candidates into the enclosing rule. Unresolved candidates contribute no declarations.

```css
@apply utilities;
```

Authoring · Tailwind-derived syntax

Defines a variant with a selector shorthand or a block containing @slot. scope(document) lets the variant select a document-level element.

```css
@custom-variant name [scope(document)] (selector);
```

Authoring · Tailwind-derived syntax

Loads a Stillwind or Tailwind CSS v4 plugin through the host. Options configure the plugin's definitions and dynamic families.

```css
@plugin '<name>' { option: value; }
```

Authoring · Tailwind-derived syntax

Marks where styled content is inserted into a variant definition.

```css
@slot;
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Places arbitrary-property candidates in the authored utility order.

```css
@stillwind-arbitrary-property pattern;
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Declares a license notice that output keeps when it contains CSS of the enclosing definition. The block contains exactly one /*! ... */ comment.

```css
@stillwind-banner { /*! Name | Author | License | URL */ }
```

Authoring · Stillwind syntax

Defines the output template selected by style.css(). A template must contain a utilities slot and cannot contain design-system definitions.

```css
@stillwind-css-template name { ... }
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Lets a plugin define a utility family on demand. The host passes undefined candidates of the family to the plugin's resolve().

```css
@stillwind-dynamic prefix-*; @stillwind-dynamic prefix-[*];
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Declares composition or value-typing metadata for matching properties.

```css
@stillwind-format property format;
```

Compiler intrinsic · Stillwind syntax

Selects a compiler intrinsic within a @stillwind-variant definition.

```css
@stillwind-intrinsic name;
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Names the theme namespace that a Tailwind v3 config key reads in theme() and in plugin configuration. extend adds the CSS values to the v3 defaults, and replace replaces them.

```css
@stillwind-legacy-theme-key fontSize --text-* extend;
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Names a legacy utility that canonical lint rewrites to its current name. A trailing * in both names keeps the rest of the name.

```css
@stillwind-legacy-utility start-* inset-s-*;
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Registers a class that candidates add to elements as written.

```css
@stillwind-marker name (modifiable);
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Registers the classes that the rules in a string select as marker classes, without emitting the rules.

```css
@stillwind-marker-source "css";
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Prunes matching theme tokens when generated CSS contains the supplied condition.

```css
@stillwind-omit-token-prefix --prefix- condition;
```

Authoring · Stillwind syntax

Registers a custom property whose registration is emitted when generated CSS requires it.

```css
@stillwind-property --name { syntax: '*'; inherits: false; initial-value: 0; }
```

Authoring · Stillwind syntax

Switches the registries that the definitions and undefinitions inside the block change. Statements outside every block change default, keyframe, and view-transition; animation starts empty. Blocks may nest, and the innermost block decides.

```css
@stillwind-registry default, keyframe, animation, view-transition { ... }
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Registers a pattern that identifies relationship candidates.

```css
@stillwind-relationship pattern;
```

Authoring · Stillwind syntax

Adds custom-property registrations to the requirements of a utility definition.

```css
@stillwind-require-properties --name;
```

Authoring · Stillwind syntax

Places generated contributions in the authored stylesheet. theme and property-initials insert declarations; utilities, keyframes, and properties insert rules.

```css
@stillwind-slot name;
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Excludes the tokens of narrower namespaces from `--value()` patterns of a namespace.

```css
@stillwind-theme-exclude --namespace-* --namespace-narrower-* ...;
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Declares a theme namespace, the value types it accepts, and optionally its scale and the fixed keys of the scale.

```css
@stillwind-theme-namespace --namespace-* [type] ... scale(key: value, ...);
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Sets the namespace order used to emit theme declarations.

```css
@stillwind-theme-order namespace ...;
```

Authoring · Stillwind syntax

Rejects arbitrary-property candidates for the matching properties in the current registries. A later @stillwind-arbitrary-property accepts them again.

```css
@stillwind-undef-arbitrary-property property | prefix-* | *;
```

Authoring · Stillwind syntax

Removes the matching utility definitions that register before it from the current registries.

```css
@stillwind-undef-utility name | prefix-* | *;
```

Authoring · Stillwind syntax

Removes the matching variant definitions that register before it from the current registries.

```css
@stillwind-undef-variant name | prefix-* | *;
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Defines a registry utility with its authored cascade order.

```css
@stillwind-utility name-* [(tw-sort: property)] { ... }
```

Registry authoring · Stillwind syntax

Defines a registry variant with optional value, modifier, scope, and ordering descriptors.

```css
@stillwind-variant name [(descriptors)] { ... }
```

Authoring · Tailwind-derived syntax

Defines design tokens or shared assets. Assets stay outside theme-token selection and resets. Inline values substitute their contents into declarations. Static values are retained without a reference.

```css
@theme [default] [asset] [inline | static] { --name: value; }
```

Authoring · Tailwind-derived syntax

Defines a utility. A trailing * captures the candidate value for --value(). The (implementation) descriptor classifies fixed declarations for lint rules with checkImplementation.

```css
@utility name-* { ... }
```

Authoring · Tailwind-derived syntax

Inside a style rule, applies each comma-separated variant sequence to a separate copy of the block. Outside style rules, a block containing @slot is accepted as a legacy variant definition. Use @custom-variant for new variant definitions.

```css
@variant variant:sequence, alternative { ... }
```
